**Claim 1.** An apparatus comprising:

a sensor interface configured to record a plurality of platform parameters characterizing an operational state of a platform;

an operator monitoring subsystem configured to record a plurality of operator actions performed in response to the recorded platform parameters;

a processor coupled to the sensor interface and the operator monitoring subsystem; and

a memory storing instructions that, when executed by the processor, cause the apparatus to generate a virtual clone of an operator based at least in part on the recorded platform parameters and the recorded operator actions, to predict, using the virtual clone, a set of expected operator actions corresponding to a current operational state of the platform, and to detect a deviation between one or more actual operator actions and the predicted set of expected operator actions.

# Patent Claims

**What is claimed is:**

1. A comparator system for managing a virtual clone and identifying parameter deviations during an activity session, the system comprising:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a memory configured to store a predetermined profile, the predetermined profile comprising a plurality of baseline parameter values associated with a subject;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a virtual clone generator, communicatively coupled to the memory, configured to instantiate a virtual clone corresponding to the subject based at least in part on the predetermined profile;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a data acquisition module configured to receive, from one or more sensors during the activity session, a plurality of real-time parameter values associated with the subject;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a comparator engine, communicatively coupled to the data acquisition module and the virtual clone generator, configured to:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;compare, in substantially real time, each of the plurality of real-time parameter values against a corresponding baseline parameter value of the virtual clone,

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;compute a deviation value for each said comparison, and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;identify a parameter deviation when a computed deviation value exceeds a predetermined threshold; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;an output module configured to generate a notification signal responsive to the identified parameter deviation.

2. The system of claim 1, wherein the virtual clone generator is further configured to dynamically update the virtual clone during the activity session based on the received plurality of real-time parameter values.

3. The system of claim 1, wherein the predetermined profile further comprises historical activity data associated with the subject collected during at least one prior activity session.

4. The system of claim 1, wherein the comparator engine is further configured to apply a weighting factor to each computed deviation value, the weighting factor being determined based on a relative priority of the corresponding parameter.

5. The system of claim 1, wherein the predetermined threshold comprises a plurality of tiered thresholds, and wherein the output module is configured to generate a distinct notification signal corresponding to each tiered threshold that is exceeded.

6. The system of claim 1, further comprising a machine learning module configured to adjust the predetermined threshold based on an aggregation of identified parameter deviations across a plurality of activity sessions.

7. The system of claim 1, wherein the one or more sensors comprise at least one of a biometric sensor, a motion sensor, a positional sensor, an environmental sensor, and a physiological sensor.

8. The system of claim 1, wherein the output module is further configured to render, on a display device, a graphical representation of the virtual clone alongside a graphical representation of the plurality of real-time parameter values.

9. The system of claim 8, wherein the graphical representation visually distinguishes each identified parameter deviation from parameters that are within the predetermined threshold.

10. The system of claim 1, wherein the comparator engine is further configured to generate a corrective recommendation associated with the identified parameter deviation, the corrective recommendation being derived from the predetermined profile.

11. A computer-implemented method for identifying parameter deviations during an activity session, the method comprising:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;storing, in a memory, a predetermined profile comprising a plurality of baseline parameter values associated with a subject;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;instantiating, by a processor, a virtual clone corresponding to the subject based at least in part on the predetermined profile;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;receiving, from one or more sensors during the activity session, a plurality of real-time parameter values associated with the subject;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;comparing, by the processor in substantially real time, each of the plurality of real-time parameter values against a corresponding baseline parameter value of the virtual clone;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;computing a deviation value for each said comparison;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;identifying a parameter deviation when a computed deviation value exceeds a predetermined threshold; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;generating a notification signal responsive to the identified parameter deviation.

12. The method of claim 11, further comprising dynamically updating the virtual clone during the activity session based on the received plurality of real-time parameter values.

13. The method of claim 11, further comprising applying a weighting factor to each computed deviation value, the weighting factor being determined based on a relative priority of the corresponding parameter.

14. The method of claim 11, further comprising adjusting, by a machine learning module, the predetermined threshold based on an aggregation of identified parameter deviations across a plurality of activity sessions.

15. A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by a processor, cause the processor to perform operations comprising:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;storing a predetermined profile comprising a plurality of baseline parameter values associated with a subject;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;instantiating a virtual clone corresponding to the subject based at least in part on the predetermined profile;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;receiving, from one or more sensors during an activity session, a plurality of real-time parameter values associated with the subject;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;comparing, in substantially real time, each of the plurality of real-time parameter values against a corresponding baseline parameter value of the virtual clone;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;computing a deviation value for each said comparison;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;identifying a parameter deviation when a computed deviation value exceeds a predetermined threshold; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;generating a notification signal responsive to the identified parameter deviation.

